  "reading": "With the same kept tones the search harms as often as the original tuner (16 vs 15). Its extra harms come from keeping more tones. Harms sit in a near-silent neighbouring band that the anti-hum renderer spills into; in old-007-r0 the rise (4.0e-6) is about five times the anti-hum power alone (7.4e-7), so the spill adds coherently to existing room content (likely the hum's own modulation sidebands reproduced with the wrong phase). Gain and phase choices cannot remove a spill whose ratio to the tone is fixed by the renderer; only muting the tone or changing the engine output can."
